Package: WSVAflowR
Title: Multi-Model Streamflow Simulation and Climate-Change Projection for Gauged Basins
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Kristen", "Cognac", email = "kristencognac@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Builds model inputs for a stream gauge (watershed, daily flow,
    climate forcing, basin attributes), calibrates and cross-validates several
    lumped process models (a Thornthwaite-Mather water balance with IHACRES
    routing, CemaNeige-GR4J/GR5J/GR6J, and HBV) on the same forcing and the
    same water-year folds, tests their transfer to contrasting climates with a
    differential split-sample test, and is designed to drive the calibrated
    models with downscaled climate projections. Potential evapotranspiration
    is always computed from the meteorological variables (FAO-56
    Penman-Monteith with land-cover crop coefficients) so historical and
    projected climate use one method.
